mutant: m074_sparse_vanished_did_miscount
target: segment/sparse.go
failure-mode: |
  The sparse rewrite's vanished-DID check (design §12.2 step 3) only looks
  at the blocks it already decoded: a DID that lost rows there counts as
  vanished even when an unfetched block still holds its rows. The new
  generation's header under-reports unique_did_count, which the status
  page, planSnapshot and any consumer sizing a DID set trust.
expected-detection: |
  The layer 3 oracle's held reader runs segment.VerifySealedMetadata on
  every generation it sees while current, which re-derives
  unique_did_count from the rows. TestSparseRewriteMatchesRewrite and
  TestSparseRewriteVanishedCheckFetches catch it at unit level.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

diff --git a/segment/sparse.go b/segment/sparse.go
index c33056b..29a5dec 100644
